      "media": [
        {
          "id": "video-1",
          "kind": "video",
          "url": "https://cdn1.telesco.pe/file/a0e760e54d.mp4?token=VlqAkZDa14u-Ujq3n91FrTsYHP79XlmRNjVkyakBLTmGqAwC5wsFOaXovTL5ypz1UFF5h0HKmazeR6ANEqZjHNTGZ6cnb_2n58IyU0SNSzLG_HvBeMtzUkKoFfqWLuLdZVHL9F2xtFR8CtXL73mdRueqAk3EFeZoIGK_7AFXQ9tqc6SnbA-vtVtAyDRxmxA0-ItdDkXPRc9LvmpETuaL0iyz_3v60juxa9Dw703sPEsppfBTzyKbU6sWYjF8UDX0bqSr6PZ8UnB3epkE1YxWwbHYg_llHvXsVlOhYqPfjOWR5DrRY-e_FCFXgnF6hTavQqZekgYIvhCPMGJJmMFpTg",
          "poster": null,
          "mimeType": "video/mp4"
        }
      ],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "So this beauty left this morning from Camp lejeune and I saw it fly over my yard. It was really low. I wish I had my phone out then.  Well now I'm out here cleaning my pool and there she goes. Flying right over my pool. Going back to Camp lejeune. \n\nThis aircraft is a Bell Boeing V-22 Osprey, a tiltrotor military aircraft that combines vertical takeoff capabilities with the speed of a turboprop.\n\nThe V-22 can rotate its engine nacelles to take off and land vertically like a helicopter, then convert to airplane mode for high-speed flight.\n\nIt is used by multiple branches of the U.S. military, including the Marine Corps (MV-22) and Air Force (CV-22) for special operations & combat support👀\n\nFunny story. One of the homes that I built and sold in 2012. An officer that purchased it teaches the Marines how to fly these. In our big playroom back then, I had picked out this gorgeous hanging light that was a glass airplane. I just thought it was cool for my boys... \nThe story is that he walked into that room and that was his sign. He quit his desk job at the Pentagon, purchased the house and is here working with our Marines✈️🚀🚁🫡🇺🇸",
